assistant: Subject: read unit_amount when price is missing
In vendor API version 2026-10-01, the product's `price` field was renamed to `unit_amount`, and the published spec wasn't updated. `get_product` only read `p.price`, so its `?? null` fallback quietly returned `price: null` instead of raising an error. The fix adds an optional `unit_amount` to `VendorProduct` in `src/tools/get_product.ts` and maps the price as `p.price ?? p.unit_amount ?? null`. Responses from 2026-01-01 still carry `price` and produce the same output as before, and the request sent upstream is unchanged. I treated `unit_amount` as US dollars, not cents. My only evidence is p-1001: it's 1199 in the new recording and its old `price` was also 1199. If the vendor documents a different unit, this mapping needs to change. `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm test` all pass (14 tests), including the repro test and the v1 fixture checks.

